IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `mca-seat`

-- Minors' Contracts Act 1987 (Singapore) -- LAYER 2 CASES: the seat's questions, answered on facts a minor, or
-- a person who contracted with a minor, could state.  One case at least for every exported question; the date
-- boundaries of ss 1 to 4 are tried on both sides; the mirror pair (the other party's question and the minor's
-- question on the SAME facts) must agree; and cases outside what the Act answers are asserted as NOTHING.
-- Every expected value was written from the text of the Act before the assertion was run.
--
-- The facts, in the order the seat asks them.  A date fixture is a day the contract was made.
--   9 April 1987 is not "after 9 April 1987"; 10 April 1987 is.  11 November 1993 is "before 12 November 1993"; 12 November 1993 is not.

GIVETH A DATE
`the first of March 2020` MEANS Date 1 3 2020
GIVETH A DATE
`the first of January 1980` MEANS Date 1 1 1980
GIVETH A DATE
`the eighth of April 1987` MEANS Date 8 4 1987
GIVETH A DATE
`the ninth of April 1987` MEANS Date 9 4 1987
GIVETH A DATE
`the tenth of April 1987` MEANS Date 10 4 1987
GIVETH A DATE
`the fifteenth of June 1990` MEANS Date 15 6 1990
GIVETH A DATE
`the eleventh of November 1993` MEANS Date 11 11 1993
GIVETH A DATE
`the twelfth of November 1993` MEANS Date 12 11 1993
GIVETH A DATE
`the thirteenth of November 1993` MEANS Date 13 11 1993

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Cases -- Does the Infants Relief Act 1874 still stand in the way of my contract? (s 1)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- A minor's contract made in 2020: s 1 says the 1874 Act "shall not apply" to it.
#ASSERT `Does the Infants Relief Act 1874 apply to my contract` `the first of March 2020` TRUE `I am not sure` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Made on 12 November 1993, the first day s 4 does not speak: the same.
#ASSERT `Does the Infants Relief Act 1874 apply to my contract` `the twelfth of November 1993` TRUE `I am not sure` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Made in the s 4 band and the Civil Law Act 1909 s 5 did not make s 1 applicable: s 4 shuts s 1 out, and the Act does not say whether the 1874 Act applies.
#ASSERT `Does the Infants Relief Act 1874 apply to my contract` `the fifteenth of June 1990` TRUE No EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Does the Infants Relief Act 1874 apply to my contract` `the tenth of April 1987` TRUE No EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Does the Infants Relief Act 1874 apply to my contract` `the eleventh of November 1993` TRUE No EQUALS NOTHING
-- In the band, s 5 did make s 1 applicable: the exception is met and s 1's own words operate (QA (NOTES.md, Judgment calls)).  If the person does not know, the Act does not answer.
#ASSERT `Does the Infants Relief Act 1874 apply to my contract` `the fifteenth of June 1990` TRUE Yes EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the Infants Relief Act 1874 apply to my contract` `the fifteenth of June 1990` TRUE `I am not sure` EQUALS NOTHING
-- The day before 9 April 1987 and the day after 12 November 1993.
#ASSERT `Does the Infants Relief Act 1874 apply to my contract` `the eighth of April 1987` TRUE `I am not sure` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Does the Infants Relief Act 1874 apply to my contract` `the thirteenth of November 1993` TRUE `I am not sure` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- On or before 9 April 1987: s 1 does not reach it.  Not a minor: s 1 does not reach it.
#ASSERT `Does the Infants Relief Act 1874 apply to my contract` `the ninth of April 1987` TRUE `I am not sure` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Does the Infants Relief Act 1874 apply to my contract` `the first of January 1980` TRUE `I am not sure` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Does the Infants Relief Act 1874 apply to my contract` `the first of March 2020` FALSE `I am not sure` EQUALS NOTHING

-- The first effect named in the bracket: the 1874 Act "invalidates certain contracts made by minors".
#ASSERT `Does the Infants Relief Act 1874 invalidate my contract` `the first of March 2020` TRUE `I am not sure` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the Infants Relief Act 1874 invalidate my contract` `the twelfth of November 1993` TRUE `I am not sure` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the Infants Relief Act 1874 invalidate my contract` `the first of January 1980` TRUE `I am not sure` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Does the Infants Relief Act 1874 invalidate my contract` `the fifteenth of June 1990` TRUE No EQUALS NOTHING

-- The second effect: the 1874 Act "prohibits actions to enforce contracts ratified after majority".
#ASSERT `Does the Infants Relief Act 1874 stop an action on my contract ratified after majority` `the first of March 2020` TRUE `I am not sure` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the Infants Relief Act 1874 stop an action on my contract ratified after majority` `the twelfth of November 1993` TRUE `I am not sure` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the Infants Relief Act 1874 stop an action on my contract ratified after majority` `the ninth of April 1987` TRUE `I am not sure` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Does the Infants Relief Act 1874 stop an action on my contract ratified after majority` `the fifteenth of June 1990` TRUE Yes EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Cases -- Is the guarantee of a minor's obligation still enforceable? (s 2)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- The lender holds a guarantee of a minor's loan made in 2020; the obligation is unenforceable against the minor because of minority.
#ASSERT `Is the guarantee saved` TRUE `the first of March 2020` Yes FALSE Yes `I am not sure` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The minor repudiated instead (the second limb), and the person is not sure the obligation is unenforceable.
#ASSERT `Is the guarantee saved` TRUE `the first of March 2020` `I am not sure` TRUE Yes `I am not sure` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The first day s 4 does not speak.
#ASSERT `Is the guarantee saved` TRUE `the twelfth of November 1993` Yes FALSE Yes `I am not sure` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No guarantee was given: s 2 does not save one.
#ASSERT `Is the guarantee saved` FALSE `the first of March 2020` Yes FALSE Yes `I am not sure` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The reason is not minority: s 2 does not save the guarantee.
#ASSERT `Is the guarantee saved` TRUE `the first of March 2020` Yes FALSE No `I am not sure` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Neither limb of (b): not unenforceable and no repudiation.
#ASSERT `Is the guarantee saved` TRUE `the first of March 2020` No FALSE Yes `I am not sure` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The person does not know whether the obligation is unenforceable: the Act presupposes law outside the sources.
#ASSERT `Is the guarantee saved` TRUE `the first of March 2020` `I am not sure` FALSE Yes `I am not sure` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Contract made on 9 April 1987: not "after 9 April 1987".
#ASSERT `Is the guarantee saved` TRUE `the ninth of April 1987` Yes FALSE Yes `I am not sure` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- In the s 4 band: shut out unless section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909 made s 2 applicable.
#ASSERT `Is the guarantee saved` TRUE `the fifteenth of June 1990` Yes FALSE Yes No EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the guarantee saved` TRUE `the fifteenth of June 1990` Yes FALSE Yes Yes EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the guarantee saved` TRUE `the fifteenth of June 1990` Yes FALSE Yes `I am not sure` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Is the guarantee saved` TRUE `the tenth of April 1987` Yes FALSE Yes No EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the guarantee saved` TRUE `the eleventh of November 1993` Yes FALSE Yes No EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- In the band, but no guarantee was given: the own "where" still says no.
#ASSERT `Is the guarantee saved` FALSE `the fifteenth of June 1990` Yes FALSE Yes Yes EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- FORK F8: in the band with section 5's effect not known, a "where" that fails on its own still says no (it is tested before the unknown exception).
#ASSERT `Is the guarantee saved` FALSE `the fifteenth of June 1990` Yes FALSE Yes `I am not sure` EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- The day before 9 April 1987 and the day after 12 November 1993.
#ASSERT `Is the guarantee saved` TRUE `the eighth of April 1987` Yes FALSE Yes `I am not sure` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the guarantee saved` TRUE `the thirteenth of November 1993` Yes FALSE Yes `I am not sure` EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- The guarantor's question on the same facts: not unenforceable for that reason alone.
#ASSERT `Is the guarantee unenforceable only because the borrower was a minor` TRUE `the first of March 2020` `I am not sure` TRUE Yes `I am not sure` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the guarantee unenforceable only because the borrower was a minor` TRUE `the first of March 2020` Yes FALSE Yes `I am not sure` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the guarantee unenforceable only because the borrower was a minor` TRUE `the twelfth of November 1993` Yes FALSE Yes `I am not sure` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Where s 2 does not save the guarantee, it does not say the guarantee is unenforceable either.
#ASSERT `Is the guarantee unenforceable only because the borrower was a minor` FALSE `the first of March 2020` Yes FALSE Yes `I am not sure` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Is the guarantee unenforceable only because the borrower was a minor` TRUE `the first of March 2020` Yes FALSE No `I am not sure` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Is the guarantee unenforceable only because the borrower was a minor` TRUE `the fifteenth of June 1990` Yes FALSE Yes No EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Is the guarantee unenforceable only because the borrower was a minor` TRUE `the fifteenth of June 1990` Yes FALSE Yes Yes EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Cases -- Can the court make the minor hand back property? (s 3)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- The other party's question.  A 2020 contract, unenforceable against the minor because of minority, the minor acquired the property under it,
-- and the other party thinks it just and equitable: the court has the power.
#ASSERT `Can the court make the minor transfer property to me` TRUE `the first of March 2020` Yes FALSE Yes `I am not sure` TRUE FALSE Yes EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Property that represents what the minor acquired.
#ASSERT `Can the court make the minor transfer property to me` TRUE `the first of March 2020` Yes FALSE Yes `I am not sure` FALSE TRUE Yes EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The minor repudiated the contract (second limb).
#ASSERT `Can the court make the minor transfer property to me` TRUE `the first of March 2020` `I am not sure` TRUE Yes `I am not sure` TRUE FALSE Yes EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- On the first day s 4 does not speak.
#ASSERT `Can the court make the minor transfer property to me` TRUE `the twelfth of November 1993` Yes FALSE Yes `I am not sure` TRUE FALSE Yes EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The other party thinks it is NOT just and equitable: "if it is just and equitable" fails.
#ASSERT `Can the court make the minor transfer property to me` TRUE `the first of March 2020` Yes FALSE Yes `I am not sure` TRUE FALSE No EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The other party cannot say whether it is just and equitable: the Act states no test.
#ASSERT `Can the court make the minor transfer property to me` TRUE `the first of March 2020` Yes FALSE Yes `I am not sure` TRUE FALSE `I am not sure` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Property that is neither acquired under the contract nor represents it: not given by s 3(1), and not refused.
#ASSERT `Can the court make the minor transfer property to me` TRUE `the first of March 2020` Yes FALSE Yes `I am not sure` FALSE FALSE Yes EQUALS NOTHING
-- FORK F9: other property AND the person says it is not just and equitable: the "if" that fails is tested before the property scope.
#ASSERT `Can the court make the minor transfer property to me` TRUE `the first of March 2020` Yes FALSE Yes `I am not sure` FALSE FALSE No EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The "where" fails: the person did not enter into the contract with the minor.
#ASSERT `Can the court make the minor transfer property to me` FALSE `the first of March 2020` Yes FALSE Yes `I am not sure` TRUE FALSE Yes EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The reason is not minority.
#ASSERT `Can the court make the minor transfer property to me` TRUE `the first of March 2020` Yes FALSE No `I am not sure` TRUE FALSE Yes EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The contract was made on 9 April 1987: not "after 9 April 1987".
#ASSERT `Can the court make the minor transfer property to me` TRUE `the ninth of April 1987` Yes FALSE Yes `I am not sure` TRUE FALSE Yes EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The person does not know whether the contract is unenforceable against the minor because of minority.
#ASSERT `Can the court make the minor transfer property to me` TRUE `the first of March 2020` `I am not sure` FALSE Yes `I am not sure` TRUE FALSE Yes EQUALS NOTHING
-- In the s 4 band.
#ASSERT `Can the court make the minor transfer property to me` TRUE `the fifteenth of June 1990` Yes FALSE Yes No TRUE FALSE Yes EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the court make the minor transfer property to me` TRUE `the fifteenth of June 1990` Yes FALSE Yes Yes TRUE FALSE Yes EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the court make the minor transfer property to me` TRUE `the fifteenth of June 1990` Yes FALSE Yes `I am not sure` TRUE FALSE Yes EQUALS NOTHING

-- The day before 9 April 1987 and the day after 12 November 1993.
#ASSERT `Can the court make the minor transfer property to me` TRUE `the eighth of April 1987` Yes FALSE Yes `I am not sure` TRUE FALSE Yes EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the court make the minor transfer property to me` TRUE `the thirteenth of November 1993` Yes FALSE Yes `I am not sure` TRUE FALSE Yes EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- MIRROR: the minor's question on the SAME facts gives the SAME answer as the other party's.
#ASSERT `Can the court make me transfer property to the other party` TRUE `the first of March 2020` Yes FALSE Yes `I am not sure` TRUE FALSE Yes EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the court make me transfer property to the other party` TRUE `the first of March 2020` Yes FALSE Yes `I am not sure` FALSE TRUE Yes EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the court make me transfer property to the other party` TRUE `the first of March 2020` `I am not sure` TRUE Yes `I am not sure` TRUE FALSE Yes EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the court make me transfer property to the other party` TRUE `the first of March 2020` Yes TRUE No `I am not sure` TRUE FALSE Yes EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the court make me transfer property to the other party` TRUE `the first of March 2020` Yes FALSE Yes `I am not sure` TRUE FALSE No EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the court make me transfer property to the other party` TRUE `the first of March 2020` Yes FALSE Yes `I am not sure` TRUE FALSE `I am not sure` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can the court make me transfer property to the other party` TRUE `the first of March 2020` Yes FALSE Yes `I am not sure` FALSE FALSE Yes EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can the court make me transfer property to the other party` FALSE `the first of March 2020` Yes FALSE Yes `I am not sure` TRUE FALSE Yes EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the court make me transfer property to the other party` TRUE `the fifteenth of June 1990` Yes FALSE Yes No TRUE FALSE Yes EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the court make me transfer property to the other party` TRUE `the fifteenth of June 1990` Yes FALSE Yes Yes TRUE FALSE Yes EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the court make me transfer property to the other party` TRUE `the ninth of April 1987` Yes FALSE Yes `I am not sure` TRUE FALSE Yes EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The two questions agree on every one of those facts (stated once more as an equation).
#ASSERT `Can the court make me transfer property to the other party` TRUE `the first of March 2020` Yes FALSE Yes `I am not sure` TRUE FALSE Yes EQUALS `Can the court make the minor transfer property to me` TRUE `the first of March 2020` Yes FALSE Yes `I am not sure` TRUE FALSE Yes

-- The conditions alone.
#ASSERT `Are the conditions for the restitution order met` TRUE `the first of March 2020` Yes FALSE Yes `I am not sure` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Are the conditions for the restitution order met` TRUE `the twelfth of November 1993` Yes FALSE Yes `I am not sure` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Are the conditions for the restitution order met` TRUE `the first of March 2020` `I am not sure` TRUE Yes `I am not sure` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Are the conditions for the restitution order met` TRUE `the first of March 2020` Yes TRUE No `I am not sure` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Are the conditions for the restitution order met` FALSE `the first of March 2020` Yes FALSE Yes `I am not sure` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Are the conditions for the restitution order met` TRUE `the first of March 2020` No FALSE Yes `I am not sure` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Are the conditions for the restitution order met` TRUE `the first of March 2020` `I am not sure` FALSE Yes `I am not sure` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Are the conditions for the restitution order met` TRUE `the tenth of April 1987` Yes FALSE Yes No EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Are the conditions for the restitution order met` TRUE `the tenth of April 1987` Yes FALSE Yes Yes EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- s 3(2): using section 3 does not prejudice any other remedy available to the claimant.
#ASSERT `Does section 3 prejudice my other remedy` TRUE `the first of March 2020` `I am not sure` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does section 3 prejudice my other remedy` TRUE `the twelfth of November 1993` `I am not sure` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The remedy is the s 3(1) transfer itself, or is not available: outside the wording of s 3(2).
#ASSERT `Does section 3 prejudice my other remedy` TRUE `the first of March 2020` `I am not sure` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Does section 3 prejudice my other remedy` TRUE `the first of March 2020` `I am not sure` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not "the claimant": the person did not enter into the contract.
#ASSERT `Does section 3 prejudice my other remedy` FALSE `the first of March 2020` `I am not sure` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "The claimant" is the person who entered into a contract after 9 April 1987 (FORK F5): outside that date s 3(2) names nobody, and says nothing.
#ASSERT `Does section 3 prejudice my other remedy` TRUE `the ninth of April 1987` `I am not sure` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Does section 3 prejudice my other remedy` TRUE `the thirteenth of November 1993` `I am not sure` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- In the s 4 band.
#ASSERT `Does section 3 prejudice my other remedy` TRUE `the fifteenth of June 1990` No TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does section 3 prejudice my other remedy` TRUE `the fifteenth of June 1990` Yes TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does section 3 prejudice my other remedy` TRUE `the fifteenth of June 1990` `I am not sure` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Cases -- Is the Minors' Contracts Act shut out of my contract? (s 4)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- In the band, section 5 of the Civil Law Act 1909 did not make the provision applicable: the Act is shut out.
#ASSERT `Is the Act shut out of my contract` `the fifteenth of June 1990` No EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The first and last days of the band.
#ASSERT `Is the Act shut out of my contract` `the tenth of April 1987` No EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the Act shut out of my contract` `the eleventh of November 1993` No EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The exception is met: the bar does not operate to that extent.
#ASSERT `Is the Act shut out of my contract` `the fifteenth of June 1990` Yes EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The person does not know whether section 5 made it applicable.
#ASSERT `Is the Act shut out of my contract` `the fifteenth of June 1990` `I am not sure` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Outside the window the text names (on or before 9 April 1987, or on or after 12 November 1993) the bar does not reach the contract: no (FORK F2).
-- The day before, the day itself and the day after each date.
#ASSERT `Is the Act shut out of my contract` `the eighth of April 1987` No EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the Act shut out of my contract` `the ninth of April 1987` No EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the Act shut out of my contract` `the twelfth of November 1993` No EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the Act shut out of my contract` `the thirteenth of November 1993` No EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the Act shut out of my contract` `the first of March 2020` No EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the Act shut out of my contract` `the first of January 1980` Yes EQUALS JUST FALSE
